Let e be the eccentricity of hyperbola and length of conjugate axis be $2 h$. since, vertex $(a, 0)$ bisects the join of centre (0,0) and focus $(a e, 0)$
$\begin{array}{l}$a=$\frac{a e+0}{2} \Rightarrow$e=2 \\
b^{2}=a^{2}$\left($c^{2}-1\right)=3 a^{2}
\end{array}

$\therefore$ Required hyperbola is $\frac{x^{2}}{a^{2}}-\frac{y^{2}}{b^{2}}=1\Rightarrow \quad \frac{x^{2}}{a^{2}}-\frac{y^{2}}{3 a^{2}}=1 \Rightarrow 3 x^{2}-y^{2}=3 a^{2}$

$3 x^2-4 y^2=300\frac{x^2}{100}-\frac{y^2}{75}=1$ and $3 x-m y+5=0 \Rightarrow y=\frac{3}{m} x+\frac{5}{m}$ Now, for condition of tangents: $\begin{aligned}& \mathrm{c}^2=\mathrm{a}^2 \mathrm{ m}^2-\mathrm{n}^2 \Rightarrow \frac{25}{\mathrm{ m}^2}=100 \times \frac{9}{\mathrm{ m}^2}-75 \\
& \Rightarrow \mathrm{m}^2=\frac{35}{3}
\end{aligned}$ Square of $y$ - intercept of $x$-radius $\mathrm{c}=\frac{25}{\mathrm{ m}^2}=25 \times \frac{3}{35}=\frac{15}{7}$
